        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): bound readInputFiles with size cap in capability-cli",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`readInputFiles` in `src/cli/capability-cli/media-output.ts` reads user-provided `--file` CLI argument files concurrently via `Promise.all` with no size limit. A user passing multiple large files to `openclaw image|document` capability commands would OOM the process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUnbounded `fs.readFile` on user-controlled paths is a known OOM vector. CLI input files (images, documents) should be reasonable — multi-GB files are not legitimate inputs for capability commands. Concurrent reads multiply the memory risk.\n\n## What Changed\n\nReplaced the `Promise.all` concurrent read pattern with sequential processing and an aggregate byte budget:\n\n- **Per-file cap**: 100 MiB (statSync pre-check before read)\n- **Command-wide budget**: 500 MiB tracked via a mutable accumulator\n- Files are processed one at a time, with remaining budget checked before each read\n- Exceeding either cap produces a clear error message\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 109 capability CLI tests pass:**\n\n```\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.cli.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.10 /home/0668000387/openclawCxbAsDev\n\n ✓ |cli| src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts (109 tests) 2679ms\n     ✓ canonicalizes case-only catalog model refs before local dispatch  529ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  109 passed (109)\n   Start at  10:05:38\n   Duration  8.07s (transform 2.66s, setup 439ms, import 4.69s, tests 2.68s, environment 0ms)\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 14.53s\n```\n\nThe aggregate budget prevents one `--file` invocation from allocating more than 500 MiB regardless of how many files are supplied. Sequential processing eliminates concurrent read amplification.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/cli/capability-cli/media-output.ts`: Add `MAX_TOTAL_CLI_INPUT_FILE_BYTES` (500 MiB), convert `readInputFiles` from `Promise.all` to sequential loop with budget tracking, pass budget through `readCliInputFileSafely`",
